WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.080
I'm Funada Kathleen!

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.480
My father gave me this name.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.130
He was an American war photographer.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.310
He would travel to conflict zones for work,

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.770
and one day he was injured on the job.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.750
But the one who operated on him 
was the doctor who became my mother!

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.960
My father passed away when 
I was still 4 years old, though.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:36.240
I was desperate, and I felt like I had to 
work hard enough to make up for his share.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.300
I was starting to get depressed 
after all our losses to the Gibia.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.630
But now!

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.460
Now we have Sensui, 
Kenroku, and everyone else,

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.230
which is really reassuring!

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:55.110
With Sensui and the others on our side, 
I feel like we can get through this!

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.130
Doctor! Are you okay?!

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:16.300
Adam!

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.320
Adam!

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.400
Adam!

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:38.600
No way...

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:52.880
Brian was infected with the Gibia Virus 
when he got hit by the Meteora.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.300
Brian...

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.980
<b>"Danger Zone"</b>

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.990
Wow!

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:43.090
Is that...?

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.530
Yeah. It's a shamisen.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.990
I found one on display.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.150
I had a habit of playing one 
like this after a battle was over,

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.720
as an offering to the souls of the dead 
and the broken weapons.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.520
Huh?

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.320
Mom?

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.410
Mom?!

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.420
What's wrong?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:14.760
I can't find my mother!

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.000
Mom!

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.560
Yurika-dono!

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.780
Mom!

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.540
Yurika-san!

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:35.790
Oh, my.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.300
Look, it's an exhibition on samurai.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.790
Th-This is!

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.800
<b>Suigetsumaru</b>

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.800
No, it can't be...

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:49.560
Could it...?

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.810
What's the matter, Sensui?

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.060
Look at this.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.820
Well, isn't that an
interesting twist of fate?

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:05.320
Never thought I'd see it 
again in a place like this.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.820
Master...

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.200
Douzan...

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.460
<i>We're finally reunited again.</i>

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.960
You've crossed countless eras 
to return to my hand,

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.260
Suigetsumaru.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:28.090
To think you'd come and find 
and me here, Douzan...

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.720
You truly are my friend.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:36.230
Oh, my, you all look so happy.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:41.880
<i>Is this a coincidence?</i>

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.650
Famous Sword Exhibit

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.200
You're a dual wielder, Sensui?

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:56.330
Yes. I received my katana 
from my barbarian master.

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:57.960
It's Suigetsumaru.

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:04.170
And this one is Halbert, 
named after my master.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.240
That reminds me, Sensui,

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:11.720
I always thought you moved 
pretty strangely, for a samurai.

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.470
Who won in the end?

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.640
That time, it was a draw.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:24.230
If we'd kept going, I would have won!

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.280
Wh-What?!

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:36.920
What's going on?!

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:43.540
You three have come at a great time!

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:47.910
Lizards?!

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:50.650
They're swarming everywhere!

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.550
Mom!

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.160
<i>Master...</i>

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:07.570
Don't stand still! Run!

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:09.300
Okay!

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:25.620
They'll surround us easily here!

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.540
We should get outside!

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:33.800
Hurry!

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:46.060
What is this?

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.280
The rain made it darker,

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.820
so now there's this many outside?!

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.910
The Doctor and the others will be 
here to meet us soon, too!

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:12.670
Here comes Kanzaki Sensui!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.960
That's an incredible number of birds.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.760
This darkness is bad!

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.440
Kathleen and the others might...

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.950
Those birds are abnormally close together.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:30.800
Over there?!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:01.660
The tools I'm used to using 
really cut the best!

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.010
Divine punishment!

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:25.080
My blood's boiling, Douzan!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.490
You're all incredible!

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.040
Everyone, hurry!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.560
Doctor, there they are!

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:19.120
Kath!

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.050
Wow.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:32.080
So, that's Sensui when he's serious, huh?

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.830
Mom, let's climb down quick!

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.170
Kathleen!

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.140
Adam?!

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:01.700
Yeah!

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.140
Hurry! We're getting out of here!

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.450
Listen up, everyone!

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:14.360
We're making a straight dash 
for the camper!

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.560
Sensui, are you okay?!

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:23.830
Yes.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:27.230
I just strained myself a bit.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.120
Run!

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.710
Damn it!

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:17.210
Sensui, don't push yourself so hard 
that you hurt yourself like this.

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:20.670
"Appearing like dew..."

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.630
Wait, what came next?

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.680
"...and fading away like dew—
such is my own life.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:32.470
Even Naniwa's splendor 
is a dream within a dream."

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.040
Mom!

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:37.550
It's a poem that describes how life 
is as ephemeral as dew

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:43.600
and, once it's over, it's little 
more than a passing dream.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:48.200
That was the Imperial Advisor's poem, right?

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.250
A dream within a dream.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:54.830
After uniting the nation, 
Toyotomi Hideyoshi must have felt

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.800
the fleetingness of life 
as his death drew near.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:02.210
When did that monkey unite the nation?!

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:10.370
<i>It was right after the
 Imperial Advisor died, wasn't it?</i>

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.340
<i>That was when I met you.</i>

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>1599       Kyoto</b>

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:19.310
<i>After unifying the nation,</i>

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.720
<i>the retired Imperial Advisor, 
Toyotomi Hideyoshi, fell ill.</i>

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:27.360
<i>The year after he breathed his last,</i>

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:32.060
<i>his death spurred the Council of Elders 
 to call back the samurai</i>

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:37.780
<i>dispatched on the first 
and second invasions into Korea.</i>

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:45.010
<i>Kanzaki Sensui, who earned the name
 "Slayer of Thousands" during the second invasion,</i>

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:48.720
<i>was no exception and he was 
forced to return home</i>

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.010
<i>with no real conclusion to the war.</i>

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:00.120
What's that?

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.910
How old has your kid gotten now, again?

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:12.060
It hasn't fallen out.

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.040
Yeah, it's there.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.930
How many times are you going to check?

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:20.630
Well, you bought it for me, after all.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.290
As proof of our marriage.

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:25.800
I'll buy you an even better one someday.

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:28.140
That's not the matter here.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.240
This is special to me.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:32.550
Jeez, you just don't get it.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:35.120
Scary.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:05.520
A dual wielder, huh?

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:08.160
Kenroku?

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:14.680
<i>This is how Sensui and Kenroku,</i>

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:20.090
<i>the samurai and ninja protecting 
Kathleen from Gibia in the modern era,</i>

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:23.320
<i>first met each other.</i>

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.470
<i>The year was 1600.</i>

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:30.190
<i>The battle that would determine the fate 
of the nation, the Battle of Sekigahara,</i>

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:34.100
<i>was quickly drawing near.
Toyotomi's vassals were divided</i>

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:37.010
<i>into the Western Army centered 
around Ishida Mitsunari,</i>

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:39.500
<i>and the Eastern Army led by Tokugawa Ieyasu.</i>

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:43.380
<i>Many of his vassals struggled 
to decide which side to take.</i>

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:49.380
<i>Matsumoto Jouzen, the man Sensui served, 
was one such vassal.</i>

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:52.130
S-Sensui!

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:58.640
I can't bring myself to betray 
the Toyotomi clan we owe so much to.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:03.140
However, didn't you promise to side 
with the Minister of the Interior?

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:03.100
<b>Minister of the Interior
(AKA Tokugawa Ieyasu, Eastern Army)</b>

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:05.910
I-I know I did, but...

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:11.650
I just can't see how the Western Army 
won't win this upcoming battle.

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:14.360
If Tokugawa-dono disappears
from this world, too,

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:17.550
then that promise will be worthless, right?

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:20.160
Then, we'll side with the Western Army, right?

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.430
Y-Yes...

00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:27.670
If that's the case, we must
inform Tokugawa Hidetada-dono.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.500
H-Hold on, Sensui!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.620
If we tell him we won't be able to join him

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.180
after keeping him waiting this long...

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.270
But if we're siding with the Western Army

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:40.460
and we tell them we're unable 
to participate in the siege of Ueda Castle,

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:42.930
we will be branded traitors.

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:45.850
Besides, unless we send
 a messenger on a fast horse

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:48.980
<b> Sanada Masayuki 
(Western Army, Toyotomi Side)</b>

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:49.950
to Sanada Masayuki at Ueda Castle at once,
 they won't make it in time!

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:53.220
I-I know that! I know that, but...

00:16:56.950 --> 00:17:03.500
<i>Tokugawa Ieyasu's third son, 
Tokugawa Hidetada,</i>

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.340
<i>led an army from Edo along Nakasendo 
to subjugate Shinano-no-kuni.</i>

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:09.620
<i>One of their goals 
was the fall of Ueda Castle,</i>

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:12.160
<i>the castle of the Sanada family, 
who had sided with the Western Army.</i>

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:18.520
<i>At the time, Jouzen had promised 
to join Ieyasu and the Eastern Army.</i>

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:23.050
<i>His troops, led by Sensui, 
were standing by near Ueda Castle</i>

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:26.160
<i>in order to join Hidetada's forces.</i>

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:30.860
Th-The enemy is the Eastern Army!

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:33.490
N-No, the W-Western Army!

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:40.220
My lord! The enemy is indeed 
the Western Army, then?!

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:41.990
Are you certain?!

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:48.610
As you wish!

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:59.830
We shall now follow Tokugawa-dono's army 
and march on Ueda Castle!

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:01.760
Our enemy is the Western Army!

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:04.780
Remember, the Western Army!

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:09.770
All units, move out!

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:16.710
<i>In this era, the most important thing 
to a daimyo wasn't duty or humanity,</i>

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:18.380
<i>but reputation.</i>

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:24.770
<i>Samurai were forced to risk their 
lives in battle to maintain face.</i>

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:31.040
<i>Now, no matter which army wins, 
we'll be branded as traitors!</i>

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:48.810
That's...

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.420
That's that man from before!

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:02.100
He fights with an interesting style.

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:06.120
So, that's the dual-wielding 
Slayer of Thousands.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:10.030
<i>During the Siege of Ueda Castle,</i>

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:12.730
<i>the attackers struggled to break 
Ueda Castle's sturdy defenses</i>

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:16.580
<i>and Hidetada was ordered to march on</i>

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:19.600
<i>before a proper resolution could be reached.</i>

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:23.700
<i>Hidetada rushed to Sekigahara,</i>

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.650
<i>but he did not make it in time 
for the main battle.</i>

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.550
<i>This earned him Ieyasu's ire.</i>

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:35.360
We may not have won the battle,

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:39.630
but hopefully Hidetada-dono 
will remember us well.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.840
<i>No... There's no chance of that.</i>

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:48.160
<i>Hidetada-dono rushed off to Sekigahara,</i>

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:50.920
<i>but he left us standing by 
at the castle alone...</i>

00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:55.220
<i>Our delay will be to blame this time.</i>

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.300
What?!

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:17.600
I am Sanada Kenroku!

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:21.110
The battle may have ended prematurely,

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:23.090
but if you've sided with the Eastern Army,

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:28.630
then I would like a duel with the 
famous Slayer of Thousands!

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:43.550
<i>Damn, strong and a dual wielder.</i>

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:47.130
<i>What an unusual samurai.</i>

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:53.060
My sword is a fusion of a samurai's soul 
and a barbarian's techniques.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:57.060
My katana will slice your flesh
and my sword will sever your bones!

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.070
I am Kanzaki Sensui!

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:11.450
<i>He evaded them?</i>

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.000
<i>Impossible.</i>

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:15.930
Didn't expect the vertical one last.

00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:17.910
You're incredible.

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:33.390
Kanzaki Sensui, Slayer of Thousands.

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:36.940
I see. You are strong.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:40.650
If we keep going any further, 
neither of us will walk away intact.

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:43.330
We'll revisit this match next time!

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:46.710
Maybe we'll see each other again, 
if we survive!

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:48.150
Farewell!

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:54.250
Sanada Kenroku, huh.

00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:06.260
Brian!

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:12.730
Oh, no!

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:20.220
What happened?!

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:22.110
We've stopped!

00:22:26.910 --> 00:22:30.110
Gibia heard the sound 
of the punctured tire!

00:22:32.300 --> 00:22:36.270
They just keep coming one 
after another, without end!

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:40.730
<i>Oh, well.</i>

00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:44.320
We both drew the short straw, didn't we?

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:46.630
Got that right.

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:57.540
Sensui's still resting up.

00:22:58.100 --> 00:23:01.440
Guess we get to handle the birds.

00:23:05.140 --> 00:23:06.100
What's that?!

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:16.450
What? What's with all those lizards?!

00:23:21.180 --> 00:23:26.000
I think we might all die here.

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:40.390
<b>"Evil VS Bushido"</b>
